# 011: Accurate CLI built-in gadget documentation (light)

## Why

The CLI command overview describes a nonexistent TellUser completion option,
and Quick Start omits the speech gadget. Readers need both pages to explain
the existing gadgets and the conditions for interactive questions accurately.
Related to WAT-1050.

## What

- Correct the agent section of `packages/docs/src/content/docs/cli/commands/overview.mdx`
  and Built-in Gadgets in `packages/docs/src/content/docs/cli/getting-started/quick-start.mdx`.
- Explain AskUser, TellUser, Finish, and TextToSpeech using
  `packages/cli/src/agent-command.ts` and `packages/cli/src/builtin-gadgets.ts` on dev.
- Explain interactive input/output requirements and the distinct disable flags.
- Decisions: one atomic documentation change with a light spec and changelog;
  use source tracing and existing mocked tests, with no new prose-pinning tests.
  Combined-light execution is authorized; scope and execution proceed together.
  Research skipped: the source of truth is existing repository code.

## Out of scope

- Other documentation pages, runtime behavior, APIs, stored shapes, dependencies,
  test changes, cross-spec decisions, and developer guidance.
- Independent PR review, remote CI, merging, issue closeout, releases,
  package publication, and promotion remain with the manager.

## Acceptance Criteria

1. [manual] Both pages describe all four gadget roles; TellUser displays messages,
   Finish signals task completion, and TextToSpeech converts text to speech audio.
   The overview removes the nonexistent TellUser.done option. Prose accuracy
   requires semantic review against source rather than a text snapshot.
2. [manual] Both pages explain that AskUser requires interactive stdin and stdout,
   is unavailable with piped input/output, and is disabled by
   `--no-builtin-interaction`; `--no-builtins` disables default built-in registration.
   Manual review checks the distinction against the registration conditions.
3. [manual] The delta contains only the two scoped doc sections and normal
   delivery artifacts. Manual diff review checks the editorial boundary.
4. Build, typecheck, lint, unit tests, coverage, mocked E2E, fresh-context local
   review, and the spec done-gate pass with normal commit hooks.

## Execution (TDD task list)

### 1. Establish behavior before editing

**Tests first**: run existing `packages/cli/src/builtin-gadgets.test.ts` and
`packages/cli/src/agent-command.test.ts`. Expected green: existing behavior
already supplies the four gadgets and completion signal. Expected doc mismatch:
the overview claims `done=true`, and Quick Start lists only three gadgets.
Trace the AskUser registration guard before writing the flag explanation.
No runtime change or permanent test is needed for this prose correction.

**Implementation**: correct only the agent options/table and adjacent explanation
in the overview, and the Built-in Gadgets section of Quick Start. Add one
`changelog.d/wat-1050-cli-builtin-gadget-docs.md` fragment.

### 2. Verify and deliver

Run the manual protocols, stage intended files, run all six target checks
sequentially, obtain `agent-plugins__z:local-review` in gate mode, run the
done-gate, and complete this spec. The spec and lock ride with the first
documentation commit; use Conventional Commits and normal hooks. Deliver
one PR to dev through the existing publication hook.

## Manual Verification

- AC #1: read both gadget tables against `getBuiltinGadgets`, each schema and
  execute function in `builtin-gadgets.ts`, and the TextToSpeech factory it imports.
  Expected: four roles match source; completion belongs to Finish, with no
  TellUser.done instruction in either page.
- AC #2: compare both explanations against the `options.builtins` registration
  block and AskUser guard in `agent-command.ts`. Expected: interactive stdin
  and stdout required; each disable flag has its own accurately stated effect.
- AC #3: inspect the diff against the locked base. Expected: only the scoped
  doc sections, this spec, and one changelog fragment; no assertions removed.

## Documentation Impact

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `packages/docs/src/content/docs/cli/commands/overview.mdx` | Correct agent gadget roles and flag semantics |
| `packages/docs/src/content/docs/cli/getting-started/quick-start.mdx` | Complete gadget list and interaction conditions |

## Verification

Run `npm run build`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`,
`npm run test:coverage`, and `npm run test:e2e` sequentially; all must exit 0.
Use mocked tests only, with no provider calls. Run the spec done-gate after
all Progress criteria are verified; commit with normal hooks.

